{"fresh_for":["Independent multi-project navigation validation"],"handover":{"confirmed_facts":["Message 14657 accepted by c8653e0b-5a45-4084-a0b9-e6c1d91de0c2: opening another project's conversation leaves a misplaced tab in the current project; clicking it switches projects.","User described projects illustratively as FOOBAR and BARFOO and is unsure exactly which link/opening route caused the issue.","App-wide responsiveness owner remains ed695f49-366e-4612-8a51-81bebbf7e2ce with mandatory Bitter Lesson reading.","Orange-attention and side-panel controls owner remains 51939cf2-c67a-4297-92be-2457306bd9e5."],"constraints":["Keep handoffs brief and let agents choose implementation intelligently.","Conversation tabs must belong to the correct project; linked opening must not contaminate the originating tab list.","Future created agents use --yolo; preserve active workflows during validation/rollout.","Separate lead-succession assignment remains discussion-only."],"open_questions":["Triggering navigation route and underlying tab-state defect remain to be confirmed.","Implementation and installed-behavior verification remain pending."],"tried_and_failed":[]},"reason":"The navigation specialist already owns cross-window conversation routing; this dispatcher retains the exact new symptom and concise-handoff preference.","recommendation":"reuse","reuse_for":["Route link, project-tab, and notification-navigation follow-ups to c8653e0b-5a45-4084-a0b9-e6c1d91de0c2","Coordinate overlaps with current responsiveness/UI owners"]}

