{"fresh_for":["Independent review of an implemented phase"],"handover":{"confirmed_facts":["Reader copies live in /opt/projects/out/hosted-machine-plan-2026-10-28 (registered in out/_reader/regenerate.py SOURCES, README and out/manifest.yaml); they are snapshots, not live links to the repo.","launchd spawn of net.tailffa31c.research-reader stuck in xpcproxy under load ~350 and swap 31.5/32 GB; the agent was booted out and serve.py runs directly under nohup (PID 28175) until logout, when launchd loads it again at login.","Mac had 1,351 processes including 170 node_repl and 170 mcp-grafana; none were killed."],"constraints":["Plan only: no AWS resources until the owner approves."],"open_questions":["The 13 owner questions in the plan."],"tried_and_failed":["launchctl kickstart -k and bootout/bootstrap of the reader agent both left the new process stuck in xpcproxy for minutes."]},"reason":"This conversation holds the plan's evidence chain and review history; the reader copy is a snapshot of commit 1ccc21b.","recommendation":"reuse","reuse_for":["Revising the plan after owner feedback","Coordinating phase 0 and phase 1 implementation"]}

Root12cd116 publishes a waiting-lock handoff for17428;97 focused tests pass, including boundary acquisition and pause/consumed-source revalidation. Activation and reply delivery remain blocked by Agent Coord runtime-owner-unavailable; no job/peer notice was submitted and direct checks, locks and reservations remain intact.
Restore availability of the existing Agent Coord runtime so the bounded handoff and requested result reply can be registered.
{"assignment_message_id":17428,"fresh_for":["Independent kernel design or precision review"],"handover":{"confirmed_facts":["Root12cd116 is pushed. Added --wait-for-selection: blocks on the same dispatch flock in a bounded managed job, then uses the normal selector and fresh validation. Periodic ticks remain nonblocking.97 focused tests pass.","Initial holders: projection73152 and attention96844. Both finite owner runners acquire dispatch+worker locks through cooldown/full CLI completion, explaining missed periodic handoffs. Projection finished naturally; attention then acquired the boundary.","No active process interrupted, no source replay, no reservation/claim/lock deleted. MoE rows26b7c444/ff275b2d were owner-authorized and source validation passed per17428.","Scope declaration, both deferred peer notices and managed job registration failed with runtime-owner-unavailable. Read-only database inspection confirmed no okc_ranked_handoff_17428 job and no peer notices. Native checkpoint MCP remains available.","Documented bounded command in private/judge/README.md: job start --job-id okc_ranked_handoff_17428 --timeout1800 --wake-self --continue... -- python3 scripts/campaign_scheduler.py --wait-for-selection.","Private evidence is under private/judge/validation/starvation_17428/. Publication encountered a live shared index.lock; bounded retry is pending. Never remove another agent's index lock."],"constraints":["Use the existing coordination runtime only; do not start a second owner, impersonate another session or edit coordination databases.","Only existing eligible owner-ranked rows may run. Preserve90s account pacing, reserves, source/owner/header checks, dedup and all uncertain reservations.","Scope declaration was rejected, but changed paths are controls-owned scheduler/tests/private judge docs. Peer owner runner source was only read."],"open_questions":["Availability of existing Agent Coord runtime for managed activation and reply delivery.","Whether natural completion of the final direct runner permits normal periodic MoE dispatch before the managed handoff can register."],"tried_and_failed":["Periodic nonblocking selection repeatedly lost to direct owner runners.","Managed handoff registration and peer notices were rejected by runtime-owner-unavailable; nothing was submitted.","Private publication hit concurrent git index.lock; retried without deleting the lock."]},"reason":"The lock-starvation diagnosis and tested operator handoff are complete; the remaining execution/delivery requires the existing coordination owner to become available.","recommendation":"reuse","reuse_for":["Register the bounded handoff and inspect MoE dispatch","Complete the requested17428 result delivery"]}

Committed 1f949aa (per-thread SQLite connection reuse, event-stream coordination reads capped at 1/s, parallel thread/session reads on open, tiling guard narrowed to conversations whose drafts move) and installed Ribbon Field 0.1.3 build 8 without stopping agents. Interface fixes are live (first open 0.85 s visible / 1.1 s loaded vs 5.5–15.9 s before); backend payload 0.1.3+8 is pending idle handover, so backend CPU (~305%) and search (2.8–8.2 s) are unchanged until it activates.
Runtime activates pending backend payload 0.1.3+8 when agents are idle (active turns and a pending approval/question currently block it); then re-measure backend CPU, search, and refresh
{"assignment_message_id":14351,"fresh_for":["Unrelated feature work","Composer behavior changes owned by the composer specialist"],"handover":{"confirmed_facts":["Root cause: backend ~350% CPU, ~270% kernel; CoordinationStore._connection opened a new SQLite connection per operation and each parsed the full schema; sample showed schema parse >3x query execution.","SSE loop reran completions/messages/sends/snoozes/approvals reads on every provider delta (~22 events/s), about 5 iterations/s per window at ~185 ms each.","Offline on snapshot: background load 237 -> 77 ms/s and new connections ~150/s -> 0 with 1f949aa.","Installed build 8 (interface live via runtime ui._WEB_ROOT switch); runtime PID 2317 instance 55dab95a unchanged; pending payload 3800bbb9 = 0.1.3+8 contains the backend fixes.","After install: first open 0.85 s visible/1.1 s loaded (was 5.5-15.9 s); reopen visible 0.06 s, loaded 1.8-2.0 s (was ~7 s). Backend still 305% CPU; search 2.8-8.2 s until handover.","Harness scripts: /tmp/rf_perf_20261029/harness (WebKit, read-only), /tmp/rf_perf_20261029/tools (offline profilers)."],"constraints":["Do not stop agents or force the backend handover; it activates at idle.","Other sessions have uncommitted edits in store.py (constructor retry) and desktop/macos; commit only own hunks.","Local builds: non-standalone via /Users/walle/.pyenv/versions/3.12.7/bin/python3, next build number must be >8."],"open_questions":["Refresh-timeout cause is partly code-derived: read() waits on the per-thread lock held by send()/update()/answer() across provider RPCs (30 s RPC timeout); not directly reproduced.","No local Sending echo was added; composer keeps text until acceptance. Send stays disabled while an open refresh is in flight.","5-second 5.2 MB thread-list poll per window and search listing all threads remain; reassess after handover."],"tried_and_failed":["Removing the full read() from send() was rejected: tests in test_browser_wake/test_browser_queue/test_app_agent_failures use read() inside send() as a Stop/pause race point."]},"reason":"This agent holds the measured baselines, harness scripts, and the pending-handover state; validating the backend once 0.1.3+8 activates needs the same before/after method and context.","recommendation":"reuse","reuse_for":["Re-measure backend CPU, search, open and refresh after payload 0.1.3+8 activates","Follow-up responsiveness fixes in store.py, ui.py, app.js, or thread-panes.js"]}

Delivered and verified live: Ribbon Field 0.1.3 build 16 is installed without stopping agents, and Enter-to-visible on the live app is p50 1.9 ms, max 7 ms (was p50 1.39 s, max 2.77 s). Backend fixes (send path, shared list build, Claude Code reuse, wake index, search 10–45x faster) are committed (097634c, 83e4e64, 21ea669, 891f5d9), pass the full suite (1,756 OK), and are staged as pending payload 852d522c; they activate automatically at the runtime's next idle handover, and until then live send acceptance remains about 1 s, shown as Sending.
The runtime activates staged backend payload 852d522c at its next idle handover (currently busy with active turns); no agents need to be stopped.
{"assignment_message_id":14625,"fresh_for":["Unrelated UI features","Independent review of the responsiveness commits"],"handover":{"confirmed_facts":["Live before (build 10/11): Enter->visible p50 1.39 s, max 2.77 s; acceptance p50 1.80 s, max 3.13 s (12 sends, probe c1d875d3, now closed). Live after build 15/16 UI: visible p50 1.9 ms, max 7 ms; acceptance p50 0.96 s (old backend still active).","Causes: no local echo; per-window 5.4 MB list rebuild on ~1.7 events/s convoying the GIL (~7 threads queued live); ClaudeRPC restarted Claude Code when developerInstructions (embedding the saved checkpoint) changed; search did 2 inventory builds plus per-row Python UDFs under a write lock; cross-project reopen awaited the list.","Final gate (realistic profile, committed code): send p50 23 / p95 230 ms, delivery p50 7 ms, list p50 3 ms, read p50 35 ms, search p50 93 ms; search p95 1.17 s only from one-time context cache build on first search.","Runtime pid 39713 instance 0737dd6f preserved through installs of builds 14, 15, 16 (ordinary Quit + build.py --install + open). Active payload 6b590466 (build 10); pending 852d522c (build 16); busy: active turns.","Commits: 7955304 (previously installed but uncommitted 01a185ba/01a185b0 fixes), 097634c, 83e4e64, 21ea669, 891f5d9. Full Python suite 1756 OK on the search commit; JS 989 OK.","The old backend serves only web files listed in its ui.py; the echo class therefore lives in app.js (83e4e64)."],"constraints":["Do not stop agents or force a backend handover; backend fixes wait for idle.","Uncommitted store.py startup-retry hunks, test_store.py, docs/runtime-updates.md, plugin.json, runtime_live_acceptance.py belong to other agents.","Plugin refresh not rerun by me: it copies the dirty tree including others' uncommitted store.py work; entrypoints route through the live runtime payload."],"open_questions":["Live acceptance and search numbers after the idle handover activates payload 852d522c are not yet measured.","First uncached conversation open still disables Send until history loads (seconds under load); overview render (555 cards) precedes conversation paint on project switch.","One Python process hosts every provider stream and request; at 2x load acceptance p95 ~0.7 s."],"tried_and_failed":["Per-thread SQLite connection pool: measured fresh connection ~0.6 ms; no list/detail difference, rejected.","First harness runs started event streams at completion cursor 0, replaying all completions and inflating backend CPU; fixed to use config completionCursor.","Poll-only harness windows did not reproduce the live storm; windows must refresh on events like app.js.","Separate outgoing-messages.js returned 404 from the old backend (build 14); moved into app.js."]},"reason":"This session holds the measured causal chain, the harness and browser driver, the before/after baselines (live and snapshot), and the deployment state, including why the backend half is pending and how web assets are served by the old backend.","recommendation":"reuse","reuse_for":["Verify responsiveness after the backend handover activates payload 852d522c","Residual latency reports (send acceptance, reopen, search)","Next structural step: moving provider adapters out of the request process"]}

