Diagnosed Ribbon Field slowness: the machine is out of memory (16 GB RAM, 27.9/28.7 GB swap used). RF's own processes account for ~16.6 GB: WebKit Networking 8.7 GB, which grows in step with three never-closed SSE streams (~7.8 GB delivered), plus Codex app-server 4.9 GB. The backend also burns 220–300% CPU on redundant SQLite I/O: a fresh connection per operation, full scans, multi-MB history rewrites, and full 4.5 MB thread-list refetches on every streamed event. Recommended fixes, in order: reload windows now, recycle SSE streams, filter list refreshes and slim the list payload, then pool connections, index app_control_requests, and coalesce history writes. No code changed yet.
Reload Ribbon Field windows (Cmd-R) to test whether WebKit Networking memory drops, and decide whether to implement the recommended fixes.
